{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And the chief cupbearer did not remember.</b> That very day." "<b>And he forgot him.</b> Afterward. Because Joseph pinned his hope on him to remember him, he was made to remain imprisoned two additional years, as it says: ״אַשְׁרֵי הַגֶּבֶר אֲשֶׁר שָׂם ה׳ מִבְטַחוֹ וְלֹא פָנָה אֶל רְהָבִים״ (Psalms 40) — and did not trust in Egypt, which is called Rahav."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:50.562637438Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}